<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-TNT tops turnover as KPN seen buying.</title>
<headline>RTRS-TNT tops turnover as KPN seen buying.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in takeover target TNT Ltd topped turnover in morning trade on Tuesday with 10.66 million shares traded.</p>
<p>The bulk of the trade was in two lines crossed through County Natwest, one of 6.5 million and one of 2.0 million, both at a price of A$2.43 per share.</p>
<p>The TNT transport group is currently under an agreed takeover offer from Dutch postal and telecoms group Koninklijke PTT Nederland NV.</p>
<p>KPN is offering A$2.45 per TNT ordinary share, valuing TNT at about A$2.0 billion.  -- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
